WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:06.985
Narrator: BLACKPINK is the hottest

00:00:06.985 --> 00:00:08.801
act in global music right now.

00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:12.150
The Korean dancing,
singing, and rapping quartet

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:15.830
got over 56 million views
in less than 24 hours

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:17.890
for their hit single "Kill This Love."

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:20.260
Now, this makes it the
largest video premiere

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.230
on the platform,

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:24.670
just barely beating out Ariana
Grande's "Thank U, Next."

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.640
Don't know who they are?
Let me get you up to speed.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:29.160
BLACKPINK consists of members

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.020
Jisoo, Jennie, Rosé, and Lisa.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:35.770
They debuted on August 8,
2016, as the second girl group

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:37.180
of YG Entertainment

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.490
and have been breaking records ever since.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.900
Their single "Boombayah" set the record

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.217
as the most-viewed debut
music video by a Korean act.

00:00:45.217 --> 00:00:50.200
"Ddu-Du Ddu-Du" debuted at 55
on Billboard's Hot 100 list,

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.140
making this the first time
a K-pop girl group ranked

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:55.357
the chart with a non-English song.

00:00:55.357 --> 00:00:58.040
"Ddu-Du Ddu-Du" is also
the most-viewed music video

00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:59.940
by a K-pop group on YouTube,

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:03.540
but they may break their own
record with "Kill This Love."

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:07.030
Their singles "Whistle"
and "Boombayah" hit No. 1

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:10.227
and 2 on the Billboard
World Digital Songs Chart.

00:01:10.227 --> 00:01:12.300
"As If It's Your Last" was ranked on

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:16.200
YouTube's Global Top 25
Songs of the Summer for 2017,

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.580
and their EP, "Square
Up," debuted at number 40

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.460
on the BillBoard 200 Charts.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:22.940
BLACKPINK has topped the charts in

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:25.570
South Korea, China, and Japan.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:26.810
With only five singles,

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:29.130
they've gotten international attention.

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:31.070
They're the first K-pop
group to be invited

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:32.390
to perform at Coachella,

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:35.010
and their performance will be
livestreamed in Times Square,

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:37.290
so yeah, they're a big deal.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:39.790
Let's get to know the
members a little bit better.

00:02:26.615 --> 00:02:29.530
In addition to being loved
for their pop and EDM sound,

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:32.100
BLACKPINK's music is
also known for their trap

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.610
and hip-hop elements.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:36.290
Now, K-pop has been accused
of cultural appropriation

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:37.250
in the past,

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:40.020
but BLACKPINK told Billboard
that they understand

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.158
the pressure of adopting a style pioneered

00:02:42.158 --> 00:02:44.450
by black American artists.

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:46.040
They're known for their authentic,

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:49.430
fun, stylish, bada--, and mature image

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:51.970
while being less concerned
with appearing perfect

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:53.800
both on and offstage.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.380
Their music is empowering,

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.370
and they have changed
the classic love stories

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:59.480
commonly associated with K-pop,

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:01.360
making themselves the decision-makers

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.150
in romantic relationships.

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:04.190
After Coachella,

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:06.330
they'll begin their North
American leg of their tour

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:09.370
and visit major cities
in the US and Canada.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.450
Now, their fanbase is called "Blinks," so

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:12.610
do you think you'll become one?

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:14.310
Let us know in the comments below.

